{
  "opening": "This release introduces several new capabilities for iterable manipulation, focusing on grouping transformations, callback-based iteration control, and sequence utilities. The following requirements define the observable behavior of the public API changes that must be delivered in this version.",
  "requirements": [
    {
      "id": "m05",
      "text": "The function groupby_transform must accept a reducefunc argument to apply a reduction operation to each group's values during transformation."
    },
    {
      "id": "m06",
      "text": "The function callback_iter must wrap an iterable to allow external interruption via a callback mechanism, exposing AbortThread, callback, done, is_sorted, result, and stagger as part of its interface or related utilities."
    },
    {
      "id": "m10",
      "text": "The function last must support receiving a reversed iterable to return the last element of such sequences correctly."
    },
    {
      "id": "m12",
      "text": "The function windowed_complete must be available as a public utility, and callback_iter must remain exposed with its associated controls."
    }
  ],
  "closing": "Please ensure all listed public names are accessible at the module level and behave according to these specifications without internal implementation details leaking into the API contract."
}
